original_text: ['*s in the lower right-hand corner are set to the number of untapped forests you sacrifice when Wood Elemental is brought into play.', 'All black creatures in play are destroyed.', 'All creatures blocked by target wall are destroyed at the end of combat.', 'All creatures blocking target attacking creature become tapped. Target attacking creature and all creatures blocking it deal no damage during combat.', 'All creatures get -1/-0 until end of turn.', 'All creatures lose flying ability.', 'All creatures now require an upkeep cost of o1 in addition to any other upkeep costs they may have. If the upkeep cost for a creature is not paid, the creature is destroyed.', 'All creatures that block or are blocked by Leprechaun become green creatures. Use counters to indicate changed creatures. Cost to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creature remains entirely unchanged.', 'All creatures with toughness 3 or less blocking target creature or blocked by target creature are destroyed at end of combat. At the end of the turn put a +1/+1 counter on the target creature for each creature destroyed in this manner during the turn. Counters remain on creature even if enchantment leaves play.', 'All creatures, lands, and artifacts played by opponent come into play tapped.', 'All enchantments on target creature are destroyed. Target creature cannot be further targeted by instants, sorceries, or enchantments.', 'All green or white creatures blocking or blocked by Abomination are destroyed at the end of combat.', 'All instants and interrupts are countered unless their caster pays an additional o\\nX, where X is the casting cost of the spell being cast.', 'All legends become tapped when Arena comes into play. Legends do not untap as normal during the untap phase.', 'All non-black creatures are destroyed. Hellfire does X + 3 damage to you; X is the number of creatures placed in the graveyard.', 'All non-wall creatures blocking Medusa are destroyed at the end of combat, as are all creatures blocked by Medusa.', 'All players bury one target non-artifact creature under their control, if they have any, during their upkeep.', 'All players may attack with no more than two creatures each turn and block with no more than two creatures each turn.', 'All players play with the cards in their hands face up on the table.', 'All players shuffle their hands into their libraries, and then draw the same number of cards they originally held.', 'All players with plains under his or her control gains 1 life point during upkeep.', 'All spells cast are countered unless their casters pay an additional o3.', 'All walls able to block Marble Priest must do so. Walls able to block more than one creature can still do so. If blocking wall is compelled to block more creatures than it is legally able to, defender chooses which of these attacking creatures to block, but must block as many creatures as it legally can. Damage dealt to Marble Priest from walls during combat is reduced to 0.', 'All your Kobolds gain +0/+1 and Trample.', 'All your Kobolds gain +1/+0.', "All your Kobolds of Kher Keep gain +2/+2. Pay o\\nRo\\nRo\\nR during your upkeep, or Rohgahh and all Kobolds of Kher Keep become tapped and come under opponent's control.", 'All your black legends gain bands with other legends.', 'All your blue legends gain bands with other legends.', 'All your creatures gain +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'All your green creatures gain +0/+2.', 'All your green legends gain bands with other legends.', "All your lands untap. Reset can only be played on an opponent's turn after his or her upkeep phase.", 'All your red legends may band with other legends.', 'All your walls gain +1/+0 and banding.', 'All your white legends gain bands with other legends.', 'Allows caster to sacrifice a swamp to regenerate a target black creature.', 'Any damage dealt to Enchanted Being during combat by creatures with one or more enchantment cards played on them is reduced to 0.', 'Any damage dealt to target creature for remainder of turn is reduced to 0.', "Any player may discard a card from hand at any time. If that player discards a land, Land's Edge does 2 damage to target player of the discarding player's choice.", 'As long as the only creatures you control are white or artifact creatures all your creatures gain +1/+1.', 'At the end of combat take control of all creatures that blocked The Wretched. The Wretched does not tap or untap these creatures. You lose control of these creatures if The Wretched leaves play or if you lose control of The Wretched.', 'At the end of your upkeep, the * below is set to the number of creatures in your graveyard.', 'Attacking does not tap target creature.', 'Backdraft does half of the damage (rounded down) done by one sorcery cast this turn to the caster of the sorcery.', 'Banding\\noc\\nT: Artifact effect which requires an activation cost is countered unless its controller spends o\\nW. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'Bartel Runeaxe cannot be the target of enchant creature spells. Attacking does not cause Bartel Runeaxe to tap.', 'Both players may take any permanent in their hand and put it directly into play. Players take turns playing one card from their hand until neither wants to play more permanents. No other spells or effects of any kind may be used while Eureka is in effect. If a spell has an X in its casting cost, X is 0.', 'Cannot be blocked by any creatures except walls and flying creatures.', "Caster may change target creature's color to any other color. This ability is played as an interrupt. Limit of one change per turn. Cost to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creature remains entirely unchanged.", "Chain Lightning does 3 damage to one target. Each time Chain Lightning does damage, the target or target's controller may then pay o\\nRo\\nR to have Chain Lightning do 3 damage to any target of that player's choice.", 'Changes the color of one or more target creatures to black until end of turn. You choose which and how many creatures are affected. Cost to tap, maintain, or to use a special ability of target creatures remains entirely unchanged.', 'Changes the color of one or more target creatures to blue until end of turn. You choose which and how many creatures are affected. Cost to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creature(s) remains entirely unchanged.', 'Changes the color of one or more target creatures to green until end of turn. You choose which and how many creatures are affected. Cost to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creatures remains entirely unchanged.', 'Changes the color of one or more target creatures to red until end of turn. You choose which and how many creatures are affected. Cost to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creatures remains entirely unchanged.', 'Changes the color of one or more target creatures to white until end of turn. You choose which and how many creatures are affected. Costs to tap, maintain, or use a special ability of target creatures remain entirely unchanged.', 'Counter target artifact effect, which must require an activation cost.', 'Counter target summon spell.', 'Counters target interrupt or enchantment. Can only counter spells that target a permanent under your control.', 'Counters target interrupt or instant spell.', 'Counters target spell. At the beginning of your next main phase, add o\\nX to your mana pool, where X is the casting cost of target spell.', 'Creatures attack and block as normal, but none deal any damage. All attacking creatures are still tapped. Play any time before attack damage is assigned.', "Creatures blocked by Wall of Dust cannot attack during your opponent's next turn. Use counters to mark these creatures.", 'Creatures may attack or use abilities that include the oc\\nT symbol during the turn they are brought into play.', 'Creatures with forestwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'Creatures with islandwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'Creatures with mountainwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'Creatures with plainswalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', "Creatures with power greater than 2 may not be assigned to block Kithkin. Blocker's power may be increased after blocking has been assigned.", 'Creatures with swampwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'Damage Wall of Shadows receives from creatures it blocks is reduced to 0. Effects that target only walls may not target Wall of Shadows.', 'Damage done to Wall of Vapor by creatures it blocks is reduced to 0.', 'Damage done to target creature by creatures it blocks, or that block it, is reduced to 0. Creature deals no damage during combat.', 'Damage done to target wall by attacking creatures is added to your life point total.', 'Damage from one sorcery spell is redirected to its caster.', 'Destroy target artifact. You gain life points equal to casting cost of artifact.', "Destroy target blue permanent or return target island to owner's hand. Enchantments on target land are destroyed.", "Destroy target red permanent, or return target mountain to owner's hand. Enchantments on target land are destroyed.", 'Destroys all forests in play.', 'During your upkeep, Gabriel gains one of the following abilities until your next upkeep: flying, first strike, trample, or rampage: 3.', 'During your upkeep, if an opponent controls more land than you, you may search your library and remove up to three basic land cards and put them into your hand. Reshuffle your library afterwards.', 'Each player may choose to be healed to 20 life. Any player choosing to be healed antes an additional card from the top of his or her library. Remove this card from your deck before playing if you are not playing for ante.', 'Elder Spawn cannot be blocked by red creatures. Sacrifice one of your islands during your upkeep or Elder Spawn does 6 damage to you and is buried.', "Every time a player draws a card, that player must first discard a card from his or her hand. If there are no cards in player's hand, take top card from library and place it in the graveyard instead of drawing. This enchantment does not apply to the first card drawn by a player during the draw phase.", 'First strike', 'First strike, Legendary Land-walk.', 'First strike, flying.', 'First strike\\nAll your Kobolds gain first strike.', 'First strike\\nCreatures with islandwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'First strike\\nCreatures with plainswalk or forestwalk may be blocked as if they did not have either ability.', 'First strike\\nCreatures with swampwalk may be blocked as if they did not have this ability.', 'First strike\\nPay o3o\\nBo\\nBo\\nB during your upkeep or Cosmic Horror does 7 damage to you and is destroyed.', 'Flip Star onto the playing area from a height of at least one foot. Star must turn at least 360 degrees or it has no effect. When Falling Star lands, Falling Star does 3 damage to each creature that it touches. Any creatures damaged by Falling Star that are not destroyed become tapped.', 'Flying', 'Flying, Rampage: 2\\nPay o\\nBo\\nUo\\nW during your upkeep or Chromium is buried.', 'Flying, Trample\\nPay o\\nWo\\nGo\\nR during your upkeep or Palladia-Mors is buried.', 'Flying, o\\nGoo\\nG First strike until end of turn.', 'Flying, oo\\nB +1/+0 until end of turn. No more than o\\nBo\\nB may be spent in this way per turn.', 'Flying\\nAn opponent damaged by Nicol Bolas must discard entire hand. Ignore this effect if opponent has no cards left in hand. Pay o\\nUo\\nBo\\nR during your upkeep or Nicol Bolas is buried.', 'Flying\\nAt the end of any turn in which a creature is placed in the graveyard from play, put a counter on the Vultures. Remove two counters to give Vultures +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nAttacking does not cause Zephyr Falcon to tap.', "Flying\\nIf Phoenix is placed in the graveyard from play, return it to owner's hand instead. It may not be summoned again until owner's next turn.", 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature to give Fallen Angel +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\no\\nGo\\nGo\\nGoc\\nT: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Flying\\no\\nGo\\nRo\\nBoc\\nT: Target player draws one card.', 'Flying\\no\\nGo\\nRoc\\nT: Target creature gains +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\no\\nGoc\\nT: Add o\\nR to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'Flying\\no\\nRoc\\nT: Manticore does 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', 'Flying\\noo\\nB Gain +1/+0 until end of turn.\\noo\\nR Gain +1/+0 until end of turn.\\noo\\nG Gain +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nPay o\\nBo\\nRo\\nG during your upkeep or Vaevictis Asmadi is buried.', 'Flying\\noo\\nG +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\noo\\nW +0/+1 until end of turn.\\nYour untapped creatures gain +0/+2. Attacking creatures do not get this bonus. Pay o\\nWo\\nGo\\nU during your upkeep or Arcades Sabboth is buried.', "For each point of damage done to you from target creature Backfire does one point of damage to target creature's controller.", 'For every point of damage target creature does, you gain 1 life.', 'Forestwalk', 'Giant Turtle may not attack if it attacked during your last turn.', 'Ichneumon Druid does 4 damage to any opponent casting an instant. This does not apply to the first instant cast by that opponent in each turn.', "If Floral Spuzzem attacks an opponent and is not blocked, then Floral Spuzzem may choose to destroy a target artifact under that opponent's control and deal no damage.", 'If Johan does not attack and is not tapped, any of your creatures may attack without tapping.', 'If Mummy is placed in the graveyard from play, remove it from the game.', 'If Scorpion damages opponent, opponent gets a poison counter. If opponent ever has ten or more poison counters, opponent loses game.', 'If Wall of Caltrops and one or more other walls join to block an attacker and no other creatures besides walls block that attacker, Wall of Caltrops gains banding ability until end of turn.', 'If a player does not cast a spell or put a card into play on his or her turn, no creatures may attack that player until after his or her next turn.', 'If any player has less than four cards in hand at the end of his or her upkeep, Storm World does one damage to that player for each card less than four.', 'If opponent casts a Summon spell that does not match the color of one of the creatures under your control, that spell is countered unless the caster pays an additional o\\nX where X is the casting cost of the Summon spell.', 'If target creature is placed in graveyard this turn, bring a creature from that graveyard directly into play under the control of the owner of the target creature. Treat this creature as though it were just summoned.', "If target creature is placed in the graveyard, return creature to owner's hand. All enchantments on target creature are destroyed. You may pay o\\nUo\\nUo\\nU to return Puppet Master to its owner's hand if target creature returns to its owner's hand.", 'If target land becomes tapped, it is destroyed at the end of the turn.', 'If your opponent controls at least as much land as you do, he or she must sacrifice a land for each land he or she puts into play.', 'Islandwalk', 'Jovial Evil does 2 damage to opponent for each white creature he or she controls.', 'Mountainwalk, protection from white.', 'Must attack each turn if possible. Gains +1/+1 at end of your upkeep. Use counters. Then pay o1 per counter or Ooze deals 1 damage to you for each counter and becomes tapped.', 'Non-flying creatures cannot attack.', 'None of your creatures can attack except for Evil Eyes. Evil Eye can only be blocked by walls.', 'None of your non-artifact creatures may attack except Akron Legionnaire.', 'On the turn during which Hag is placed in the graveyard, all creatures who dealt damage to Hag that turn become 0/2 creatures. Use counters to mark these creatures.', 'On your next upkeep after Hazezon is put into play, put * token Sand Warriors into play, where * is the number of lands under your control. Treat the Warriors as 1/1 white, green, and red creatures. If Hazezon leaves play, all Sand Warriors are also removed from game.', 'Pay 1 each time target creature attempts to attack, block, or tap. That action is prevented and the creature becomes tapped. Destroy enchantment if mana is not paid.', 'Pay o3 during your upkeep or Forethought Amulet is destroyed. If you receive more than 2 damage from a sorcery or instant source, that damage is reduced to 2.', 'Pay up to o2 less than required whenever casting a summon spell.', 'Pay up to o2 less than required whenever casting an instant, interrupt, or enchantment spell.', 'Plainswalk', "Play after combat is over. All surviving creatures blocked by target wall this turn are buried. For each creature buried in this manner, choose one creature from attacker's graveyard and return it to play under attacker's control. Treat these creatures as if they were just summoned. If there are not enough creatures in attacker's graveyard, all creatures in attacker's graveyard are returned to play.", 'Play before defense is chosen. Target creature gains first strike until end of turn. If the creature does not already have rampage, then it also gains rampage: 2 until end of turn.', 'Protection from black', 'Protection from black\\nGains +1/+1 (use counters) at the end of each turn in which it does damage to opponent.', 'Protection from red\\nAll guardians gain +1/+1 if an opponent controls any red cards.', 'Protection from red\\nGains +1/+1 if an opponent controls any white cards.', 'Protection from white\\nDamage done to wall by creatures with enchantment cards played on them is reduced to 0.', "Psychic Purge does 1 damage to any target. If a spell cast by opponent or a permanent under opponent's control causes you to discard this card, opponent loses 5 life. Effects that prevent or redirect damage may not be used to counter this loss of life.", "Put X counters on one target creature that target wall blocked during this turn; X is the power of the blocked creature. Creature does not untap as normal while it has one or more of these counters on it. Remove one counter during creature's controller's upkeep.", "Put X counters on target creature. Target creature becomes tapped when Venarian Gold is cast. Creature does not untap as normal if it has any of these counters on it. Remove one counter during creature's controller's upkeep phase.", 'Put a -0/-2 counter on target creature every time it becomes tapped. Counters remain even if enchantment is removed.', "Put a 0/-1 counter on target creature during its controller's upkeep. If the creature is placed in the graveyard, its controller chooses a new target for Takklemaggot. If there are no legal targets, Takklemaggot becomes an enchantment and does 1 damage to the controller of the last creature Takklemaggot was on, during his or her upkeep. Takklemaggot does not revert to a creature enchantment even if other creatures are afterwards brought into play.", 'Put one counter on Voodoo Doll during your upkeep. If Voodoo Doll is not tapped at end of your turn, it does X damage to you and is destroyed. X equals the number of counters on Voodoo Doll.\\no\\nXo\\nXoc\\nT: Voodoo Doll does X damage to any one target.', 'Put seven counters on Rasputin when brought into play. You may remove a counter to prevent one damage to Rasputin or add o1 to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt. Put one counter on Rasputin during your upkeep if he started the turn untapped. You may not have more than seven of these counters on Rasputin at any time.', "Put two counters on this card. Remove a counter during your upkeep. When you remove the last counter from All Hallow's Eve, all players take all creatures from their graveyards and put them directly into play. Treat these creatures as though they were just summoned. You choose what order they come into play.", 'Put two counters on this card. Remove a counter during your upkeep. When you remove the last counter from Divine Intervention, the game is over and considered a draw.', 'Pyrotechnics does 4 damage divided any way you choose among any number of targets.', 'Rampage: 1', 'Rampage: 2', 'Rampage: 3', "Remove all enchantments you control and remove all enchantment cards played on all permanents you control. If this spell is cast during opponent's attack, also remove all enchantment cards played on attacking creatures. All enchantments you own are returned to your hand; all other enchantments are destroyed.", "Return target permanent to owner's hand; enchantments on target permanent are destroyed.", 'Sacrifice X cards from your hand and then bring X cards from your graveyard to your hand. Then remove Recall from the game.', "Sacrifice a creature during your upkeep to gain life equal to creature's toughness.", 'Search your library for any one basic land and put it into play. This does not count towards your one land per turn limit. Reshuffle your library afterwards.', 'Storm Seeker does 1 damage to opponent for every card in his or her hand.', 'Swampwalk', "Swampwalk\\nSol'kanar's controller gains 1 life each time a black spell is cast.", 'Switch target enchantment from one creature to another or from one land to another. The controller of the enchantment does not change. New target of enchantment must be valid or this spell has no effect. Treat this as if the enchantment had just been cast on the new target.', 'Sword of the Ages comes into play tapped.\\noc\\nT: Sacrifice Sword of the Ages and as many creatures as you choose. Sword does the combined power of these creatures in damage to one target. Sacrificed creatures and Sword are then removed from the game entirely.', 'Syphon Soul does 2 damage to all players except caster. Caster gains life points equal to the amount of damage done by Syphon Soul.', 'Tap land enchanted with Equinox to counter a spell that destroys one or more of your lands. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'Tap target creature you control and put three counters on it. Target creature does not untap as normal while it has one or more of these counters on it. Remove one counter during your upkeep. During the upkeep phase after the one in which the last counter was removed, Cocoon is destroyed and target creature gains a +1/+1 counter and flying ability.', 'Target attacking creature comes under your control untapped. Return to former controller at end of turn. This creature is no longer considered to have attacked. Play before defense is chosen.', 'Target creature cannot be blocked by any creatures except white creatures and artifact creatures.', 'Target creature cannot be blocked until end of turn. Play after attack is declared and before defense is chosen.', 'Target creature cannot be the target of instants, sorceries, fast effects, or enchantments unless creature is tapped.', "Target creature deals no damage during combat but gains X toughness until end of turn; X is target creature's casting cost.", "Target creature deals no damage during combat this turn. Creature becomes tapped and may not untap as normal during its controller's next two untap phases.", 'Target creature deals no damage during combat. Creature cannot attack.', "Target creature gains +0/+X until end of turn where X is the creature's casting cost.", 'Target creature gains +1/+0\\no\\nRo\\nRoo\\nR Regenerates', 'Target creature gains +2/+2', 'Target creature gains +2/-2.', 'Target creature gains +3/+3.', "Target creatures gain +4/-4 until end of turn. If this reduces creature's toughness below 1, creature's toughness is 1.", 'Target player and caster each choose one of the creatures they control with the highest casting cost. Exchange control of these creatures. Then do the same for artifacts. Juxtapose does not tap or untap these cards. The control of any enchantment cards played on these permanents is unchanged. If one player does not have an artifact or creature do not trade that type of card.', 'Target player gains X life or prevents X damage to any one creature or player.', 'Target spell is countered unless its caster spends an additional o1.', "Target untapped creature you control becomes tapped. Add an amount of colorless mana equal to target creature's casting cost to your mana pool.", 'Target wall you control gains +10/+0 when blocking. Any damage dealt to target wall is reduced to zero. Target wall is destroyed at end of turn.', 'The * in the lower right hand corner is 1 when cast. While blocking, you may choose to change * to equal one plus the power of target creature sentinel blocks this turn. While attacking, you may choose to change * to equal one plus the power of target creature that blocks Sentinel this turn.', 'The *s below equal the number of lands you control.', "The top card of each player's library is always face up.", 'This card is a red spell when cast and Kobolds are a red creature.', 'Trample\\nDamage done to Bronze Horse by spells which target it is reduced to zero as long as you control another creature.', 'Trample\\nEach time a creature is placed in the graveyard during a turn in which Axelrod damaged it, you gain 1 life and Axelrod does 1 damage to target player.', 'Trample\\nRampage: 2', 'Trample\\nWurm cannot attack until it has been assigned as a blocker.', 'Treat all land in play as both lands and 1/1 creatures. They may not be tapped for mana the first turn they are brought into play.', 'Typhoon does 1 damage to each opponent for each island he or she controls.', 'Underworld Dreams does one damage to opponent for each card he or she draws.', 'Until end of turn, damage done to target creature by spells or effects that target it is reduced to 0.', "Until end of turn, target creature's power and toughness are switched. Effects that alter power alter toughness instead, and vice versa.", 'When Clergy are destroyed or take lethal damage, unless opponent pays o1 Clergy are regenerated.', 'When Halfdane comes into play he is 3/3. During your upkeep, Halfdane acquires the current power and toughness of target creature other than Halfdane. If there are no legal targets, Halfdane becomes 3/3.', 'When Mold Demon is brought into play, controller must sacrifice two swamps or Mold Demon is buried.', 'When Stangg is brought into play, also put a Stangg Twin token into play. Stangg Twin token is a 3/4 green and red legend. If Stangg leaves play, remove Stangg Twin token from game. If Stangg Twin leaves play, bury Stangg.', 'When placed in the graveyard from play, Effigy does 3 damage to target creature. If an Effigy is damaged by another Effigy in this manner and is placed in the graveyard that turn, it deals the amount of damage received from the other Effigy in addition to its normal 3.', 'When target artifact is tapped, the controller of Relic Bind can choose to do 1 damage to any player or give 1 life to any player.', 'While Presence of the Master is in play, any new enchantments cast are countered.', 'Wombat gains +2/+2 for each creature enchantment on it. Attacking does not cause Rabid Wombat to tap.', 'X target creatures become tapped. Winter Blast does 2 damage to each target creature that has flying.', 'X target creatures gain islandwalk until end of turn.', "You gain 1 life point each time one of opponent's mountains becomes tapped.", 'You may draw two extra cards during your draw phase, then either put two of the cards drawn this turn back on top of your library (in any order), or lose 4 lives per card not replaced. Effects that prevent or redirect damage may not be used to counter this loss of life.', 'You may look at the top five cards of any library. You may then choose to shuffle that library.', 'o1: +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'o1: +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'o1o\\nGoc\\nT: Target creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', 'o1oo\\nW Prevents all damage against you from one red or black source. If a source does damage to you more than once in a turn, you must pay o1o\\nW each time you want to prevent the damage.', 'o2o\\nBo\\nRoc\\nT: Put a minor demon token into play. Treat this token as a 1/1 red and black creature.', 'o2o\\nGoo\\nG Put a Wolves of the Hunt token into play. Treat this token as a 1/1 green creature with the ability bands with other Wolves of the Hunt.', "o2o\\nUo\\nUoc\\nT: Return target permanent to owner's hand. Cannot target permanents with enchantment cards played on them.\\nIf Time Elemental blocks or attacks it is destroyed and does 5 damage to controller.", 'o2o\\nUoo\\nU Gain +4/-4 and allow Wall of Wonder to attack this turn.', 'o2oc\\nT: Change the color of target permanent you control to a color of your choice. Use counters. Cost to cast, tap, maintain, or use a special ability of card remains unchanged.', 'o2oc\\nT: Put one counter on Black Mana Battery.\\noc\\nT: Add o\\nB to your mana pool. Remove as many counters as you wish. For each counter removed add o\\nB to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o2oc\\nT: Put one counter on Blue Mana Battery.\\noc\\nT: Add o\\nU to your mana pool. Remove as many counters as you wish. For each counter removed add o\\nU to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o2oc\\nT: Put one counter on Green Mana Battery.\\noc\\nT: Add o\\nG to your mana pool. Remove as many counters as you wish. For each counter removed add o\\nG to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o2oc\\nT: Put one counter on Red Mana Battery.\\noc\\nT: Add o\\nR to your mana pool. Remove as many counters as you wish. For each counter removed add o\\nR to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o2oc\\nT: Put one counter on White Mana Battery.\\noc\\nT: Add o\\nW to your mana pool. Remove as many counters as you wish. For each counter removed add o\\nW to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o2oc\\nT: Take a card from your library without looking at it and place it face down under Knowledge Vault. Sacrifice Knowledge Vault to discard entire hand and take the cards under the vault into your hand. If Knowledge Vault leaves play, put all cards under it in your graveyard.', 'o2oc\\nT: Target creature deals no damage during combat this turn.', 'o2oc\\nT: Target creature you control deals no damage this turn, but gains +0/+X until end of turn, where X is the casting cost of target creature.', 'o3oc\\nT: Counter target interrupt or enchantment. Can only counter spells which target a permanent under your control. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'o3oc\\nT: Put one counter on Triassic Egg. If there are at least two such counters, you may sacrifice Triassic Egg to take any creature from your hand or graveyard and put it directly into play. Treat this creature as though it were just summoned.', "o3oc\\nT: Redirect damage done to you from one source to target creature of opponent's choice.", 'o4oc\\nT: During your upkeep, put one counter on target creature. You may remove this counter at any time to regenerate that creature.', 'o4oc\\nT: Put a Poison Snake token into play. Treat this token as a 1/1 artifact creature. If this creature damages opponent, opponent gets a poison counter. If opponent ever has ten or more poison counters, opponent loses game.', 'o4oc\\nT: You may cast one spell this turn by paying its casting cost with any type of mana. For example, o2o\\nGo\\nG becomes o4. However, the card still retains its original color. This ability is played as an interrupt.', "o5: During controller's next upkeep Giant Slug gains landwalk ability of controller's choice until end of turn. The type of landwalk chosen must correspond with one of the five basic land types.", 'o5: Sacrifice Gauntlets of Chaos. Take control of target land, creature, or artifact. Then give former controller of that permanent control of a target permanent of the same type under your control. You each control these permanents until game ends. Gauntlets of Chaos does not tap or untap these permanents. Enchantments on traded permanents are destroyed.', 'o5oc\\nT: Prevents all damage done to you by attacking non-flying creatures.', 'o\\nBo\\nWoc\\nT: Target creature does no damage during combat this turn.', 'o\\nBoc\\nT: Redirect all damage done to you from any one attacking creature to the Shimian Night Stalker.', 'o\\nBoo\\nR +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'o\\nGo\\nRo\\nBoc\\nT: Select one creature from your graveyard and place it in your hand.', 'o\\nRo\\nBo\\nBo\\nUoc\\nT: Destroy target tapped creature or target blocking creature. Tetsuo may not be a target of an enchant creature spell.', 'o\\nWo\\nUo\\nGoc\\nT: Creatures attack and block as normal, but none deal any damage during combat. All attacking creatures are still tapped. Use this ability any time before attack damage is dealt.', 'o\\nWo\\nUo\\nGoc\\nT: Regenerate target creature.', 'o\\nXoc\\nT: Name a card. Opponent reveals X cards from his or her hand at random, or entire hand if he or she does not have enough cards. Opponent then discards any of those cards that match the one you named. May only use this power during your turn.', 'oc\\nT: Add o2 to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nB to your mana pool. This ability is played as an interrupt.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nB to your mana pool\\noc\\nT: Remove first strike ability or swampwalk ability from target creature until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nG to your mana pool\\noc\\nT: Target 1/1 creature gains +1/+2 until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nR to your mana pool\\noc\\nT: Remove all landwalking ability from target creature until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nU to your mana pool.\\nThis ability is played as an interrupt.', 'oc\\nT: Add o\\nU to your mana pool\\noc\\nT: During upkeep remove the banding or bands with other ability from target creature until end of turn.', "oc\\nT: Add o\\nW to your mana pool\\noc\\nT: Return target legend to owner's hand; enchantments on target legend are destroyed.", 'oc\\nT: Archer does 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', 'oc\\nT: Destroy target blue creature.', 'oc\\nT: Destroys a target creature which has an enchantment card played on it.', 'oc\\nT: During your upkeep sacrifice a creature and take a creature from your graveyard and put it directly into play. Treat this creature as though it were just summoned.', 'oc\\nT: Gain control of target creature. Rubinia does not tap or untap this creature. If Rubinia becomes untapped you lose control of this creature; you may choose not to untap Rubinia as normal during your untap phase. You also lose control of target creature if either Rubinia leaves play or you lose control of Rubinia.', 'oc\\nT: Gain control of target legend. If Willow Satyr becomes untapped, you lose control of this legend; you may choose not to untap Willow Satyr as normal. You also lose control of legend if Willow Satyr leaves play, if you lose control of Willow Satyr, or if the game ends.', 'oc\\nT: Lady Caleria does 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', "oc\\nT: Pick a card at random from opponent's hand and place it in yours. Bury Tempest Efreet in opponent's graveyard. The change in ownership is permanent. Play as an interrupt, but opponent may prevent effect by paying 10 life or conceding game before the card to be switched is chosen—if this is done, Tempest Efreet is buried. Effects that prevent or redirect damage may not be used to counter this loss of life. Remove this card from deck if not playing for ante.", 'oc\\nT: Prevent up to 2 damage to one creature.', 'oc\\nT: Psionic Entity does 2 damage to any target but does 3 damage to itself.', 'oc\\nT: Remove the bands with other ability from target creature until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Sacrifice Mirror Universe during your upkeep, and trade your number of live points with opponent. For example, if you had 2 life points and your opponent had 10, you would now have 10 life points and your opponent would have 2. Effects that prevent or redirect damage may not be used to counter this change of life.', 'oc\\nT: Target artifact becomes tapped.', 'oc\\nT: Target artifact controlled by opponent becomes tapped or untapped.', 'oc\\nT: Target creature gets -1/-0 until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Target creature loses flying ability until end of turn.', 'oc\\nT: Target plains produces o1 instead of o\\nW until end of game. Use counters.', 'oc\\nT: Target player discards one card from his or her hand at random. This power may only be used during your turn.', "oc\\nT: Target player names a card and then turns over the top card of his or her library. If it matches the named card, the card is put in the player's hand; otherwise it is put into the graveyard.", 'oc\\nT: Tor Wauki does 2 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', 'oo\\nB Draw an extra card and lose 2 life. Effects that prevent or redirect damage may not be used to counter this loss of life.', "oo\\nB Lesser Werewolf gets -1/-0 until end of turn. Put a -0/-1 counter on target creature that blocks or is blocked by the Werewolf. Use this ability after defense is chosen but before damage is dealt. You may not use this ability to reduce the Lesser Werewolf's power below 0.", 'oo\\nB Regenerates']
